    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners`: when a request repeats an `Idempotency-Key` that already created an owner, it returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which the household-duplicate rule would otherwise reject with 409).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (not Spring MVC), the change is:\n\n**New function steps** (wired into `owners.POST.yml`):\n- `CheckIdempotentCreate` \u2014 new **first** step. Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header via `ServerHttpConnection` (null when absent/blank), looks it up in the registry, and if a prior owner exists throws a checked `IdempotentReplayException` carrying that owner's DTO \u2014 short-circuiting before the duplicate check. Unseen/missing keys fall through to the normal pipeline.\n- `RecordIdempotentCreate` \u2014 new step after `SaveOwner` (once the id is assigned). Records `key \u2192 ownerId`.\n\n**Supporting pieces:**\n- `IdempotencyRegistry` \u2014 a `@Component` holding a process-wide `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>` (`find`/`record`, storing by-first-write).\n- `IdempotentReplayException` (checked) + `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` \u2014 the handler replays the stored `OwnerDto` via `ObjectResponse<OwnerDto>` (200 by default), registered at `officefloor/escalation/\u2026IdempotentReplayException.yml`.\n\nBoth steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]` to stay in the pipeline's single transaction; the replay path writes nothing, so its rollback is harmless.\n\nDesign notes worth flagging:\n- The registry is **in-memory**, so idempotency records don't survive a restart and aren't shared across nodes \u2014 fine for this single-process app and the test, but not durable/distributed. A DB-backed table would be needed for that.\n- Header extraction is shared via a `static` helper on `CheckIdempotentCreate` to keep the two steps consistent.\n\nFull suite (`AcceptanceTest`, incl. the new `coreIdempotentRepeat`) is green.",
