    "probe_text": "I now have the full pipeline. Here is the complete, ordered account of what `POST /api/owners` does. Every step runs under one shared `transaction` governance, so all DB work commits once at the very end (or rolls back if any step throws).\n\n## Endpoint guard (before the pipeline)\n- **Authorization**: `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## 1. `checkIdempotent` \u2014 `CheckIdempotentCreate`\n- Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (trimmed; blank/absent \u2192 ignored).\n- If that key was already recorded **and** the owner it created still exists \u2192 throws `IdempotentReplayException` carrying the original owner, short-circuiting to replay the original response (no duplicate created). Unseen key, or key whose owner has vanished \u2192 falls through.\n\n## 2. `build` \u2014 `BuildOwner`\nRuns `@Valid` bean-validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` **first** (failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, 400):\n- `firstName`: `@NotNull`, letters-only pattern (up to 2 space/`'`/`-`-separated parts), size 1\u201330.\n- `lastName`: `@NotNull`, same pattern (optional trailing `.`), size 1\u201330.\n- `city`: `@NotNull`, size 1\u201380.\n- `telephone`: `@NotNull`, size 1\u201320.\n- `title`: size \u226410; `address`: size 1\u2013255; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/`email`: size \u2264255.\n- `postcode`: pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`.\n\nThen, in order, the method body:\n1. **Canonicalizes the address** \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE), composes the flat `address` (structured form preferred), and writes all three back onto the request. *(side-effect on the request/entity)*\n2. **Required-field check** (collects all missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, 400): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (must be non-empty after normalization), `city`, `telephone`.\n3. **Normalizes telephone** to E.164 (strips separators, assumes +61, drops a leading 0, enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400) on failure.\n4. **Normalizes email** \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise must match the syntactic regex or `InvalidEmailException` (400); stored trimmed + lower-cased.\n5. Maps request \u2192 `Owner` entity.\n6. **Registration date**: null \u2192 server date; a supplied **future** date \u2192 `RegistrationDateInFutureException` (400); then **rolls forward to the next business day** (skips weekends and the fixed 2026 holiday list). *(side-effect)*\n7. Computes and stamps `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; hash of telephone+lastName). *(side-effect)*\n8. Publishes the built `Owner` and a `sharesHousehold` flag for later steps.\n\n## 3. `checkEmailDomain` \u2014 `CheckOwnerEmailDomain`\n- Rejects a disposable email domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400). No-op if email absent.\n\n## 4. `checkPostcode` \u2014 `CheckOwnerPostcode`\n- If postcode present: re-checks 4-digit format, then the semantic region range from the city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4 digits) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). No-op if absent.\n\n## 5. `assignHousehold` \u2014 `AssignOwnerHousehold`\n- **Stamps `householdId`** (deterministic hash of normalized lastName + postcode) and **`householdSize`** (this owner plus existing members with the same id, from a full-repository scan). *(side-effect; no rejection)*\n\n## 6. `checkIdentity` \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`\n- Unless `sharesHousehold` is true, rejects if any **non-deleted** existing owner shares the `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## 7. `checkCityCapacity` \u2014 `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\n- Rejects if the city already holds \u226550 owners (case-insensitive count) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n## 8. `checkDailyLimit` \u2014 `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`\n- Rejects if \u2265100 owners already share the (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n## 9. `checkBulkSignup` \u2014 `CheckOwnerBulkSignup`\n- Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if >80 owners already share the registration date. *(side-effect; no rejection)*\n\n## 10. `countNamesakes` \u2014 `CountOwnerNamesakes`\n- Stamps `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive). *(side-effect)*\n\n## 11. `checkPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 `CheckOwnerPossibleDuplicate`\n- Unless `sharesHousehold`: if an existing non-deleted owner shares lastName + postcode but has a **different** telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate` = true and `possibleDuplicateOf` = that owner's id (lowest id wins). No-op without a postcode. *(side-effect; no rejection)*\n\n## 12. `dedupeCustomerCode` \u2014 `DeduplicateCustomerCode`\n- Makes `customerCode` unique against existing codes by appending `-<n>` (n\u22652). *(side-effect)*\n\n## 13. `save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the actual persistence (assigns the id). A DB constraint clash surfaces as `DataIntegrityViolationException` (has its own handler).\n\n## 14. `recordIdempotent` \u2014 `RecordIdempotentCreate`\n- Records `Idempotency-Key \u2192 owner.id` in the registry (no-op without a key), so a later repeat replays this owner. *(side-effect)*\n\n## 15. `audit` \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- Writes one line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membershipLevel, membershipNumber). *(side-effect)*\n\n## 16. `respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- Sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n---\n\n**Two things worth flagging** as you read this:\n- The idempotency guard (step 1) commits its recording only at the pipeline's end alongside everything else, but the DTO validation of `@Valid` happens in step 2 \u2014 so an invalid body still runs *after* the idempotency lookup, not before.\n- Steps 5\u201312 each perform a **full `findAll()` repository scan**, so a single create walks the entire owner table many times.\n\nLet me know if you'd like the HTTP status of any particular escalation confirmed against its handler YAML."
